## Why This Is Asked

Covers a realistic data-leak risk from IAM misconfig in pipelines, focusing on formal CAPA processes at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- Evidence-driven REST APIs
- Metrics for containment and prevention
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express route to POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body };
  caps.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you secure the CAPA API (authorization, audit logs, idempotency)?
- How would you integrate with existing incident response tools?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design with privacy considerations in data-labeling.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence and lineage
- Cross-tenant lifecycle with SLAs
- API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Privacy metrics: exposure window, recurrence rate
- RCA template and canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA type
class CAPARecord {
  constructor(id, evidence, lineage, owners) {
    this.id = id; this.evidence = evidence; this.lineage = lineage; this.owners = owners;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify exposure window in MTTI terms?
- What telemetry would you add to prove recurrence reduction after rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing automation for ML-driven incidents across regions with provenance, containment, and auditability.

## Key Concepts
- ML drift handling across regions
- Evidence, lineage, owners in CAPA data model
- Region-aware lifecycle and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and RCA templates

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  evidence: string[];
  lineage: string; // data/feature provenance
  owners: string[];
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'remediated'|'verified';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you instrument drift detectors for reliability vs latency?
- How would you automate ROI- and policy-linked approvals for canaries?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement data lineage capture across CDC and streaming layers?
- What rollback safety checks would you add to the canary plan?
